WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.500
Let's start today with an update on how the
pandemic is going in the United States and

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:11.920
around the world, this is probably the least
good update that we've had in a couple of

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.920
months.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.680
But it does require some thought and some
explanation and there's some details to understand.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.160
So the top line, like the bad number, the
number going in the wrong direction is cases.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.619
Cases per day in the United States and around
the world are now climbing once again.

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:33.140
And after more than two months of declines
and significant declines for much of that

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:40.640
to two and a half month period, average daily
cases are again ticking up not by that much,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:47.690
but from a low of about 55000 new cases a
day in the United States, now up about five

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.960
percent to 58000 cases per day.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.489
Remember context.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:58.180
These are numbers many in twenty twenty thought
we would never get to.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.850
We blew past them all the way up to two hundred
and fifty five thousand cases per day came

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.840
back down and now we're back up from 55000
to 58000.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.119
What is driving this?

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:14.009
We're vaccinating we're vaccinating millions
per day at this point and we'll look at those

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:15.009
numbers.

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:17.469
How is it that cases are again going up?

00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:19.869
A couple of different things going on.

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:27.420
One is that in some states, the more contagious
British variant known as B one one seven is

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.749
becoming more widespread.

00:01:28.749 --> 00:01:36.130
Now, remember that the vaccines work really
well against B one one seven, but among unvaccinated

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.479
people, it's going to spread more.

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:42.899
That's exactly what is happening, for example,
in Michigan, Michigan is a place where B one

00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:48.909
one seven is becoming more widespread as the
variant of of dominance.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:51.859
And Michigan's cases aren't just ticking up
slightly.

00:01:51.859 --> 00:01:56.149
They're skyrocketing primarily again among
unvaccinated people.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:02:01.969
Michigan cases are up 250 percent from a recent
low.

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:06.780
So the other aspect of this is, is more of
a sort of I guess you'd call it a psychological

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:13.269
aspect in a sense, as people learn about vaccination
and they hear that people are getting vaccinated

00:02:13.269 --> 00:02:18.329
and they hear that cases are coming down,
some people choose to behave less safely.

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:22.880
And there's an analogy here to something that
traffic engineers deal with.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.450
When traffic engineers look at a stretch of
highway, a road, for example, that has a lot

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.910
of traffic and they say we need more lanes
in order to better accommodate traffic, they

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.959
will start a project to widen the road.

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:40.060
And of course, people learn about the fact
that the road is going to be widened and will

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.790
have more capacity.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:47.959
And often what happens is that by the time
that the road is widened, increasing capacity,

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:53.170
more people, because they have heard, hey,
this road will have more capacity, so traffic

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.200
will go down, more people choose to use the
road.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.590
And so by the time that the road is done,
you have more capacity.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:04.689
But traffic is moving just as slowly because
more people are choosing to use the road.

00:03:04.689 --> 00:03:09.849
Similarly, we are seeing spring breakers in
Florida states rolling back all guidelines,

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:14.749
et cetera, as cases started to come down because
vaccination was going up and the seasonality

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:19.189
effect, more people are behaving less, less
responsibly, less safely, I guess we would

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:20.189
say.

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:22.560
And thus we are starting to see cases tick
back up.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.269
Now, despite cases going up.

00:03:25.269 --> 00:03:29.239
The good news is that deaths continue to decline
for now.

00:03:29.239 --> 00:03:33.120
As we know at this point, deaths lag cases
by about three weeks.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.700
We're already three weeks out from cases leveling
deaths continue to decline from their peak

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:46.720
of about nearly 3500 a day towards the middle
to end of January, now down to about a thousand

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.720
deaths a day.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.420
That is a decline of 70 percent.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.519
But the decline, the rate of decline is slowing
down.

00:03:54.519 --> 00:04:00.849
And one signal that might not bode so well
is in terms of people going into the hospital.

00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:08.620
New hospitalizations have also continued down,
but the rate of decline is slowing down significantly.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:13.849
So this is a crucial period of about, I would
say, two to three months is what most of the

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:15.999
epidemiologists say.

00:04:15.999 --> 00:04:19.870
It's a battle of vaccination versus variance.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.669
And we have very good data about how good
the vaccines are.

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:31.350
I read yesterday a study which tracked California
health care workers after being vaccinated.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:37.240
And what the study found was that the fully
vaccinated health care workers, meaning 14

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:44.910
days out from dose number two, something like
zero point zero five percent, became infected.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:51.319
This is a group that's highly exposed, working
in health care settings around unvaccinated

00:04:51.319 --> 00:04:56.620
sick patients, very low rate of contagion
among those who are vaccinated.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.199
So that's the good news.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:03.530
Vaccinations now averaging right around two
point five million doses per day, that's a

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:08.080
combination of two dose vaccines and a single
dose.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:13.040
Johnson and Johnson total two point five million
doses per day.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.759
That number should continue to grow.

00:05:15.759 --> 00:05:17.930
It appears that it is going to continue to
grow.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:23.349
But this is not a good time to start going
crazy the way we've seen spring breakers do

00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:24.349
in Florida.

00:05:24.349 --> 00:05:28.050
So super zoomed out, vaccinations up, deaths
down.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.259
That's good.

00:05:29.259 --> 00:05:36.210
Medium term hospitalizations leveling out,
not declining that quickly lately.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:41.710
Cases up and vaccine distribution in much
of the world, not good.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:47.740
And ultimately, I mean, to really get back
to normal as a global village, for lack of

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:52.060
a better term, other countries are going to
need to do well on vaccination.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:57.919
There are countries not expected to get significant
access to vaccines until 2023, maybe wouldn't

00:05:57.919 --> 00:05:59.900
even fully vaccinate until 2024.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.190
Who knows what variants will be on two by
then.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.139
So this is a bigger issue.

00:06:04.139 --> 00:06:09.500
Now, we're starting to hear, you know, more
about a vaccine equity and countries like

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.130
the U.S. and the U.K. hoarding vaccines and
different issues.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:18.190
As I've said before, I think it's perfectly
natural that countries would try to vaccinate

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.419
their own people first.

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:26.721
But there is no question that until there
is more vaccine distribution globally, we

00:06:26.721 --> 00:06:31.430
are not going to be able to say that we have
we have dealt with the pandemic, but let's

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.479
keep vaccinating.

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:37.569
All you can do here in the US is when you
can get a vaccine, get one.

00:06:37.569 --> 00:06:38.060
That's what you can do

